{"id":"83a9a929ecea09d7","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-thm-kato.md","title":"Kato's Inequality","display":"thm-kato — Kato's Inequality","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-kato","aliases":["58-thm-kato"],"display":"thm-kato — Kato's Inequality","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-vector-bundle.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-kato"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-kato</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-kato — Kato's Inequality"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"bb62713ade4dcadf\" href=\"?note=bb62713ade4dcadf\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-vector-bundle.md\">../batch17/58-df-vector-bundle.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,E,p,\\tau_E,\\tau_M,r,g,h,\\nu,u,\\nabla,a,D_a,D_\\nabla u,n_a,n_\\nabla u\\in V\">\\(M,E,p,\\tau_E,\\tau_M,r,g,h,\\nu,u,\\nabla,a,D_a,D_\\nabla u,n_a,n_\\nabla u\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{VectorBundle}_S(p,E,\\tau_E,M,\\tau_M,\\mathbb C,r)\">\\(\\mathrm{VectorBundle}_S(p,E,\\tau_E,M,\\tau_M,\\mathbb C,r)\\)</span> is as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"bb62713ade4dcadf\" href=\"?note=bb62713ade4dcadf\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-vector-bundle.md\">../batch17/58-df-vector-bundle.md</a>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> is as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RiemannianMeasureDatum}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\tau_M,g,\\nu)\">\\(\\mathrm{RiemannianMeasureDatum}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\tau_M,g,\\nu)\\)</span> means that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g\">\\(g\\)</span> is a smooth Riemannian metric and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu\">\\(\\nu\\)</span> its completed Riemannian volume measure.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HermitianBundleMetric}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(h,p,E,M)\">\\(\\mathrm{HermitianBundleMetric}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(h,p,E,M)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricConnection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h)\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricConnection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h)\\)</span> have their standard geometric meanings, including compatibility of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nabla\">\\(\\nabla\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h\">\\(h\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SobolevBundleSection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(u,1,2,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)\">\\(\\mathrm{SobolevBundleSection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(u,1,2,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)\\)</span> is the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"W^{1,2}\">\\(W^{1,2}\\)</span> relation for measurable sections; it is not the Euclidean scalar Sobolev-space predicate formerly cited here.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WeakKatoData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,D_a,D_\\nabla u,n_a,n_\\nabla u,u,\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)\">\\(\\mathrm{WeakKatoData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,D_a,D_\\nabla u,n_a,n_\\nabla u,u,\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)\\)</span> means, up to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu\">\\(\\nu\\)</span>-almost-everywhere representatives, that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a(x)=\\lVert u(x)\\rVert_h\">\\(a(x)=\\lVert u(x)\\rVert_h\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D_a\">\\(D_a\\)</span> is its weak differential, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D_\\nabla u\">\\(D_\\nabla u\\)</span> is the weak covariant derivative, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n_a,n_\\nabla u\">\\(n_a,n_\\nabla u\\)</span> are their pointwise metric norms.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SobolevScalarFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,1,2,M,g,\\nu)\">\\(\\mathrm{SobolevScalarFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,1,2,M,g,\\nu)\\)</span> is scalar <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"W^{1,2}\">\\(W^{1,2}\\)</span> membership on the Riemannian manifold.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kato} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{VectorBundle}_S(p,E,\\tau_E,M,\\tau_M,\\mathbb C,r)\\land\n\\mathrm{RiemannianMeasureDatum}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\tau_M,g,\\nu)\\land\n\\mathrm{HermitianBundleMetric}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(h,p,E,M)\\land\n\\mathrm{MetricConnection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h)\\land\n\\mathrm{SobolevBundleSection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(u,1,2,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)\\land\n\\mathrm{WeakKatoData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,D_a,D_\\nabla u,n_a,n_\\nabla u,u,\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)\n\\to\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{SobolevScalarFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,1,2,M,g,\\nu)\\land\n\\nu(\\{x\\in M:n_a(x)&gt;n_\\nabla u(x)\\})=0\\land\n\\bigl(\\int_M n_a(x)^2\\,d\\nu(x)\\bigr)^{1/2}\n\\leq\\bigl(\\int_M n_\\nabla u(x)^2\\,d\\nu(x)\\bigr)^{1/2}\n\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kato} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{VectorBundle}_S(p,E,\\tau_E,M,\\tau_M,\\mathbb C,r)\\land\n\\mathrm{RiemannianMeasureDatum}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\tau_M,g,\\nu)\\land\n\\mathrm{HermitianBundleMetric}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(h,p,E,M)\\land\n\\mathrm{MetricConnection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h)\\land\n\\mathrm{SobolevBundleSection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(u,1,2,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)\\land\n\\mathrm{WeakKatoData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,D_a,D_\\nabla u,n_a,n_\\nabla u,u,\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)\n\\to\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{SobolevScalarFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,1,2,M,g,\\nu)\\land\n\\nu(\\{x\\in M:n_a(x)&gt;n_\\nabla u(x)\\})=0\\land\n\\bigl(\\int_M n_a(x)^2\\,d\\nu(x)\\bigr)^{1/2}\n\\leq\\bigl(\\int_M n_\\nabla u(x)^2\\,d\\nu(x)\\bigr)^{1/2}\n\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Kato's inequality: gradient of absolute value bounded by gradient.</li>\n<li>Used in heat kernel bounds and spectral estimates.</li>\n<li>Formally: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|d|u|| \\leq |\\nabla u|\">\\(|d|u|| \\leq |\\nabla u|\\)</span> pointwise almost everywhere.</li>\n<li>The geometric Sobolev interfaces are explicitly marked metatheoretic because the Euclidean scalar Sobolev atom cannot type bundle sections, covariant derivatives, or Riemannian volume. All data needed to interpret the inequality are exposed in the theorem signature.</li>\n<li>Applications: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^p\">\\(L^p\\)</span>-boundedness of spectral multipliers.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-vector-bundle.md","status":"resolved","id":"bb62713ade4dcadf","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-vector-bundle.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-vector-bundle.md","status":"resolved","id":"bb62713ade4dcadf","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{VectorBundle}_S(p,E,\\tau_E,M,\\tau_M,\\mathbb C,r)$ is as in [[../batch17/58-df-vector-bundle.md]], and $\\mathrm{Function}$ is as in [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]].","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{VectorBundle}_S(p,E,\\tau_E,M,\\tau_M,\\mathbb C,r)$ is as in [[../batch17/58-df-vector-bundle.md]], and $\\mathrm{Function}$ is as in [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M,E,p,\\tau_E,\\tau_M,r,g,h,\\nu,u,\\nabla,a,D_a,D_\\nabla u,n_a,n_\\nabla u\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{VectorBundle}_S(p,E,\\tau_E,M,\\tau_M,\\mathbb C,r)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RiemannianMeasureDatum}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\tau_M,g,\\nu)","display":false},{"tex":"g","display":false},{"tex":"\\nu","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HermitianBundleMetric}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(h,p,E,M)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MetricConnection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h)","display":false},{"tex":"\\nabla","display":false},{"tex":"h","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SobolevBundleSection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(u,1,2,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)","display":false},{"tex":"W^{1,2}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{WeakKatoData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,D_a,D_\\nabla u,n_a,n_\\nabla u,u,\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)","display":false},{"tex":"\\nu","display":false},{"tex":"a(x)=\\lVert u(x)\\rVert_h","display":false},{"tex":"D_a","display":false},{"tex":"D_\\nabla u","display":false},{"tex":"n_a,n_\\nabla u","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SobolevScalarFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,1,2,M,g,\\nu)","display":false},{"tex":"W^{1,2}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kato} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{VectorBundle}_S(p,E,\\tau_E,M,\\tau_M,\\mathbb C,r)\\land\n\\mathrm{RiemannianMeasureDatum}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(M,\\tau_M,g,\\nu)\\land\n\\mathrm{HermitianBundleMetric}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(h,p,E,M)\\land\n\\mathrm{MetricConnection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h)\\land\n\\mathrm{SobolevBundleSection}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(u,1,2,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)\\land\n\\mathrm{WeakKatoData}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,D_a,D_\\nabla u,n_a,n_\\nabla u,u,\\nabla,p,E,M,g,h,\\nu)\n\\to\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{SobolevScalarFunction}_{\\mathsf{meta}}(a,1,2,M,g,\\nu)\\land\n\\nu(\\{x\\in M:n_a(x)>n_\\nabla u(x)\\})=0\\land\n\\bigl(\\int_M n_a(x)^2\\,d\\nu(x)\\bigr)^{1/2}\n\\leq\\bigl(\\int_M n_\\nabla u(x)^2\\,d\\nu(x)\\bigr)^{1/2}\n\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"|d|u|| \\leq |\\nabla u|","display":false},{"tex":"L^p","display":false}],"bytes":2822,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4249","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-thm-kato.md|58-thm-kato]]（batch14）"}],"outgoing":["bb62713ade4dcadf","36d7463d215be751"]}